# Pull request size

A pull request’s counted diff is at most **120 lines**. Count insertions plus deletions from the merge base:

```bash
git diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD \
  ':(exclude)**/package-lock.json' \
  ':(exclude)**/go.sum' \
  ':(exclude)**/dist/**'
```

Sum column 1 and column 2. Lockfiles, `dist/`, and generated files do not count. Tests, config, rules, and docs do count.

If code plus its tests would exceed 120, split the behavior. Do not drop the test. If code plus the living-doc update would exceed 120, ship the ADR first, then the code, then the remaining doc edits, all in the same milestone.

One milestone may be several pull requests. Each branches from the default branch after the previous one in that milestone is merged.
